# Scope the knowledge graph to the BLUEPRINT (the rooms), not the raw/output layers.
#
# This mirrors the workspace's own rule (CLAUDE.md, "rooms vs projects/"): the rooms are the
# workflow and the knowledge; projects/ is user data - often stale, mid-experiment, or built
# before the current best-practice landed - and outputs/ is generated. Graphing them buries the
# ~630 markdown files that ARE the blueprint under ~16k PBIR JSON nodes.
#
# Remove a line here if you deliberately want to graph a project's report structure.

# Raw layer - user data, not knowledge
power-bi/projects/
synthetic-data/projects/

# Output layer - generated, dated artifacts
power-bi/outputs/
synthetic-data/outputs/

# Provenance snapshots - upstream reference, explicitly "do not load"
power-bi/_examples/
synthetic-data/_examples/

# Working scratch + the graph's own output
.scratch/
graphify-out/
